invalid.ts:2:5 lint/nursery/noObjectLiteralComparison ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  × This compares a value with an empty array literal.
  
    1 │ /* should generate diagnostics */
  > 2 │ if (value === ([] as string[])) {}
      │     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    3 │ if (value === ({} satisfies object)) {}
    4 │ if (value !== <object>{}) {}
  
  i Each array literal creates a new array. Comparing a value with it never checks whether the value is empty: objects and arrays are compared by reference, not by their contents.
  
  i To check whether an array is empty, use value.length === 0.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

